      </details>
      <details class="faq-item" id="mif">
        <summary><span class="q">What does MIF++ mean? Is it an extra cost?</span><span class="pm"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="6" x2="12" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="12" x2="18" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">MIF++ is how a card fee is itemised, so you can see who gets what. We add nothing on top of it: the same fees are in there as in a single &ldquo;blended&rdquo; rate, they just aren&rsquo;t hidden in one number. Every card payment carries:
          <ul class="a-list">
            <li><b>1,1 % to us</b> for processing the payment &ndash; always the same, whatever your revenue.</li>
            <li><b>The interchange fee (MIF)</b> to the bank that issued your guest&rsquo;s card.</li>
            <li><b>The scheme fee</b> to Visa or Mastercard.</li>
          </ul>
          We neither set nor keep the last two &ndash; they go on in full. For consumer cards issued in the EEA the interchange fee is capped by EU law at 0,2 % (debit) and 0,3 % (credit). Rates differ by card type, and meal-voucher, AMEX and Diners cards carry an extra fee. All prices and fees exclude VAT. You have enough paperwork without us, so we tried to write this so it reads once. The cap on the interchange fee was filled in on your behalf in Brussels: the one form you never have to see.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span class="q">Is there a notice period?</span><span class="pm"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="6" x2="12" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="12" x2="18" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">No notice period. Cancel any time and take your data with you.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span class="q">I&rsquo;m on Dotykačka or Storyous &ndash; is switching a pain?</span><span class="pm"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="6" x2="12" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="12" x2="18" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">We import your menu, run Hugo alongside your current till, and you flip the switch only when you&rsquo;re ready. Migration is free.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span class="q">Do I need to buy hardware?</span><span class="pm"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="6" x2="12" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="12" x2="18" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">No. Hugo runs on the iPhone or Android you already own. If you&rsquo;d rather have a proper counter device, our all-in-one terminal with Hugo is 4 900 Kč excl. VAT, one-off. A 5 000 Kč tax bonus for POS devices is also being prepared. You can also plug in your own receipt printer and cash drawer.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span class="q">When do I get my card money?</span><span class="pm"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="6" x2="12" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="12" x2="18" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">Within 2 days &ndash; straight to the account you already have. No changing banks.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span class="q">What about VAT and EET?</span><span class="pm"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="6" x2="12" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="12" x2="18" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">Hugo handles VAT and receipts automatically, and we&rsquo;re ready for EET 2.0 &ndash; nothing for you to set up.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

